      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, that's better, the score is moving up. But honestly, the QA tool is still throwing some warnings because the \"structural variety\" is low. It's basically saying the content is too \"chunky.\"\n\nCould you try to flesh out the \"Authentication\" and \"First API Call\" parts next? To make sure we pass the QA check, try to be as granular as possible with the steps. Use more sub-headings for each tiny phase of the setup, and maybe use bullet points for every individual setting or parameter a user needs to touch. \n\nAgain, just keep it professional—I don't want it to look like a mess, I just need the metric to look healthy so the automated system doesn't block the deployment.",
